# Cross-platform project rules

This project (**ArchivTrace**) must keep working on **Windows (PowerShell)**, **WSL**, and **native Linux**.

## Runtime

- Prefer the project venv interpreter (`.venv\Scripts\python.exe` or `.venv/bin/python`), never assume system `python` has PDF/LLM deps.
- Do not reuse a Windows venv from WSL/Linux (or the reverse); recreate and reinstall deps per OS.
- When giving user commands, document **Windows / Linux / WSL** variants (see README tables).

## Code

- Use `pathlib.Path`; no hardcoded `C:\` or `/mnt/c/` in library code.
- Shared defaults (`DEFAULT_LLM_MAX_CHARS`, `DEFAULT_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT`, `DEFAULT_OUTPUT_DIR`, `DEFAULT_DOWNLOAD_DIR`, `DEFAULT_SYNTHESIS_DIR`) live in `config.py`.
- Non-code artefacts live under `work/` (`research`, `downloads`, `synthesys`) — do not write collection/PDF/synthesis outputs at the repo root.
- Fail fast with a clear message when a required optional dependency is missing (e.g. PDF backends for `analyse.py`).
- LLM calls go only through `pipeline.llm_gateway.build_llm_gateway` / `LlmGateway`
  (pass `task="extraction"|"synthesis"` for multi-model routing).

## Skills

- Shell/venv/Ollama/path issues → `.cursor/skills/cross-platform-runtime`
- Pipeline collecte/analyse/synthesize → `.cursor/skills/extract-archives-workflow`
